greetd 0.10.3: seamless overlap handoff (default on, opt-out)

Rebased onto greetd 0.10.3 from upstream PR #6 (kennylevinsen/greetd,
"seamless overlap handoff"; fork humain-os/greetd, branch feat/global-comp).

When [general] overlap_handoff = true (now the DEFAULT, so preserved
configs without the key get it automatically on upgrade), the user session
is started on a second, inactive VT while the greeter stays live; after
overlap_switch_secs (default 3) greetd VT-switches to the session and
SIGTERMs the greeter. The session VT is chosen with VT_OPENQRY (first free
VT) instead of the fork's naive greeter-VT+1, falling back to VT+1 if the
query fails. Set overlap_handoff = false to restore the classic behavior.

Safety fix: greeters that self-exit on login success (e.g. agreety) no
longer leave a blank screen. When the greeter exits while a session is
pre-started, check_children now VT-switches to the session VT BEFORE
promoting it; previously the switch only happened in alarm(), which found
the overlap already taken and did nothing, stranding the session on an
inactive VT.

VT-mode fix: the overlap switch must not use VT_SETACTIVATE/VT_AUTO on the
session VT. logind prepares controlled graphical sessions as KD_GRAPHICS +
VT_PROCESS; forcing VT_AUTO leaves KD_GRAPHICS + VT_AUTO, which Linux ignores
for later switch-away requests. Use plain VT_ACTIVATE + VT_WAITACTIVE instead.

No new cargo dependencies; Cargo.lock is untouched.

